{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 5448 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "5f16488fbd369b045cb417c72df24f5063e1de37284060d44020b6e99b4f7a24" :edb/db-before-t 5447 :edb/db-after-t 5448 :edb/tx-data [[13194139538760 50 #inst "2026-10-22T09:44:07.385Z" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186184172 1038 #edb/ref 17592186673406 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186184172 1038 #edb/ref 17592186673411 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186184172 1038 #edb/ref 17592186673413 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186184172 1038 #edb/ref 17592186673426 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186184172 1038 #edb/ref 17592186673452 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186184172 1040 #edb/ref 17592186549300 13194139538760 17592186045443 false] [17592186184172 1040 #edb/ref 17592186673453 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673406 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673428 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673406 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673435 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673406 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673442 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673406 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673406 1071 "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix which has only $5$ non-pivot column?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673406 1072 #uuid "01c27acc-5739-59f4-8fe9-e2185b961d5f" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673406 1074 "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 5 non-pivot columns give $\\text{nullity}(A)=5.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+5=5,\\qquad \\text{rank}(A)=5-5=0.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=0$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 0. The number of pivot columns is 0, and the number of non-pivot columns is 5.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is false. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $5$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{5}.$” is false. $\\dim(\\text{Col}(A))=0$.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{nullity}(A)=5$” is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$." 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673407 1075 #edb/ref 17592186673410 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673407 1075 #edb/ref 17592186673420 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673407 1075 #edb/ref 17592186673437 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673407 1075 #edb/ref 17592186673449 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673407 1075 #edb/ref 17592186673450 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673407 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673407 1077 "selection" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673407 1078 #edb/ref 17592186673420 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673407 1079 #uuid "08b95a80-6d17-56c6-be43-c7d7451f84eb" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673408 1080 "false" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673408 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673408 1083 #uuid "08e87190-2841-5611-9c70-dc6033a40400" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673409 1080 "true" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673409 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673409 1083 #uuid "12d11e7b-2e35-5882-ae11-4fee9d03b2dc" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673410 1080 "I and III only" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673410 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673410 1083 #uuid "12f8229f-ef39-5cfa-a4bd-a0f2f936e940" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673411 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673412 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673411 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673421 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673411 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673429 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673411 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673411 1071 "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $10\\times 10$ matrix with $2$ pivot columns?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673411 1072 #uuid "1a6f89b5-17bd-5c0c-b910-92e1887d4880" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673411 1074 "Since $A$ is a $10\\times 10$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{10} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=10=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 2 pivot columns give $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n2+\\text{nullity}(A)=10,\\qquad \\text{nullity}(A)=10-2=8.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=2$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 2. The number of pivot columns is 2, and the number of non-pivot columns is 8.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is false. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{nullity}(A)=8$” is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{rank}(A)=2$” is true. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$; $\\text{rank}(A)=2$." 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673412 1075 #edb/ref 17592186673418 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673412 1075 #edb/ref 17592186673439 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673412 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673412 1077 "$\\text{rank}(A)=2$" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673412 1078 #edb/ref 17592186673439 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673412 1079 #uuid "1aff7ca8-ae95-5320-870a-283e02efa317" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673413 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673407 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673413 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673413 1071 "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix with $3$ pivot columns?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=5$\n\nII. $A$ is not invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673413 1072 #uuid "1c93f8c9-c546-50e4-a1df-c54e8f82f0eb" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673413 1074 "Since $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{8} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=8=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 3 pivot columns give $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n3+\\text{nullity}(A)=8,\\qquad \\text{nullity}(A)=8-3=5.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 3. The number of pivot columns is 3, and the number of non-pivot columns is 5.\n\n- Statement I is false. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement III is false. $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is II only." 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673414 1080 "false" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673414 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673414 1083 #uuid "2390ff3f-82fc-54bf-9b85-5082cf00aedd" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673415 1080 "true" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673415 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673415 1083 #uuid "2b01ce81-b96e-5329-acb7-60b29187eee6" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673416 1080 "true" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673416 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673416 1083 #uuid "2c3b4623-c248-5a02-b8ee-7ba16209f579" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673417 1080 "false" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673417 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673417 1083 #uuid "34b9502c-410e-52f5-b026-c2f9b31705b3" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673418 1080 "false" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673418 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673418 1083 #uuid "366e42cb-2574-576c-ae6c-5df19e16a5c9" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673419 1080 "true" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673419 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673419 1083 #uuid "3d4fbb