73425 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673425 1077 "$A$ is not invertible" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673425 1078 #edb/ref 17592186673422 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673425 1079 #uuid "56e65182-7ecd-5970-9716-4a82b7f451d7" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673426 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673424 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673426 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673438 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673426 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673440 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673426 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673426 1071 "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and  $\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ 3a \\\\ 3b\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a,b\\in R\\right\\}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673426 1072 #uuid "5b807f80-d3e7-5284-9d78-b367cb5db361" 13194139538760 17592186045443 true] [17592186673426 1074 "Since $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{3} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=3=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$  \n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe supplied null space has the independent spanning vectors\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThus $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+2=3,\\qquad \\text{rank}(A)=3-2=1.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=1$ and $\\text{nullity}(